2059
02:38:37,358 --> 02:38:50,176
这是我 200 多个最棒的免费 AI SEO 和 Chat GPT 提示词，就是我亲自使用的那些。我还加入了我的社区链接——AI Profit Boardroom，以及我的免费策略咨询页面。
It's my 200 plus best free AI SEO and Chat GPT prompts, the exact ones I use myself. I also added the link to my community, the AI Profit Boardroom, and my free strategy session page.

2060
02:38:50,286 --> 02:38:51,856
这三样就是我的源文件。
Those three things are my sources.

2061
02:38:52,174 --> 02:38:53,808
这就是为什么这很重要。
And here's why that matters so much.

2062
02:38:54,048 --> 02:38:57,728
工作室今天生成的一切内容都直接源自这些源文件。
Everything the studio makes today comes straight out of those sources.

2063
02:38:57,902 --> 02:38:58,820
这就是核心所在。
That's the whole point.

2064
02:38:59,008 --> 02:39:07,236
它只使用你提供的内容。它不会在互联网上乱跑去抓取随机的东西。它阅读你的文件并基于它们构建一切。
It only uses what you give it. It doesn't go wandering off across the internet and grab random stuff. It reads your files and it builds everything from them.

2065
02:39:07,328 --> 02:39:09,808
而且它会准确显示每一行内容来自哪里。
And it shows you exactly where each line came from.

2066
02:39:10,094 --> 02:39:14,928
你会看到一些可以点击的小标签，当你点击其中一个时，它会直接跳转到你文件中的对应位置。
You'll see little clickable chips and when you tap one, it jumps you right to that spot in your file.

2067
02:39:15,118 --> 02:39:16,368
所以思考一下这意味着什么。
So think about what that means.

2068
02:39:16,590 --> 02:39:22,768
普通的聊天机器人从它学到的所有内容中提取信息。这很强大，但它也可能出错并一本正经地胡说八道。
A normal chatbot pulls from everything it ever learned. That's powerful, but it can also get things wrong and say them with a straight face.

2069
02:39:23,008 --> 02:39:31,328
Gemini Notebook 不会那样做。它锁定在你的素材上。所以当你用它构建内容时，你可以信任它。它是基于你的内容的，而不是凭空捏造的。
Gemini Notebook doesn't do that. It stays locked to your material. So when you build something with it, you can trust it. It's grounded in your stuff, not made up.

2070
02:39:31,534 --> 02:39:38,448
而且你也不局限于 PDF。你可以给它喂 Word 文档、Google Docs、网页链接，甚至是 YouTube 视频。
And you're not stuck with PDFs either. You can feed it Word docs, Google Docs, web page links, even a YouTube video.

2071
02:39:38,670 --> 02:39:47,248
你把它粘贴进去，它就成了你可以基于此构建的源文件。所以当你访问 notebook.google 并加载自己的文件时，你放入的内容决定了产出内容的形态。
You paste it in and now it's a source you can build from. So when you go to notebook.google and load your own files, whatever you put in is what shapes everything you get out.

2072
02:39:47,408 --> 02:39:54,688
好的输入，才有好的输出。这适用于几乎所有人。如果你在学习，把你的笔记和阅读材料放进去，它就能为你生成学习资料。
Good stuff in, good stuff out. And this works for pretty much anyone. If you're studying, you drop in your notes and readings and it builds you study material.

2073
02:39:54,848 --> 02:39:58,768
如果你在做研究，丢入一堆报告，它就会提取出关键信息。
If you're doing research, you drop in a stack of reports and it pulls out what matters.

2074
02:39:58,848 --> 02:40:05,408
如果你在经营品牌，把你自己的指南、内容和笔记放进去，它可以将它们重塑为你需要分享的任何形式。
If you're running a brand, you drop in your own guides, your content, your notes, and it reshapes them into whatever you need to share.

2075
02:40:05,648 --> 02:40:07,488
同样的工具，完全不同的用途。
Same tool, totally different jobs.

2076
02:40:07,662 --> 02:40:09,188
唯一的限制就是你提供给它的内容。
The only limit is what you feed it.

2077
02:40:09,408 --> 02:40:15,876
所以，想想那个你一直想搞懂的文件或文件夹，想象一下把它放进这里。
So think about the one file or the one folder that you've been meaning to actually understand and imagine dropping it in here.

2078
02:40:16,048 --> 02:40:18,288
这是这五个功能共有的核心理念。
That's the mindset for all five of these.

2079
02:40:18,448 --> 02:40:20,448
好了，我们从幻灯片演示文稿开始。
Alright, let's start with the slide deck.

2080
02:40:20,608 --> 02:40:23,888
这个功能是全新的，而且说实话有点神奇。它到底是什么呢？
This one is brand new and honestly kind of magic. So what is it?

2081
02:40:24,048 --> 02:40:27,044
幻灯片演示文稿能把你文件变成完整的演示文稿。
The slide deck turns your files into a full presentation.

2082
02:40:27,248 --> 02:40:31,888
带有标题、要点和图片的真实幻灯片。而且它只需要大约一分钟就能完成。
Real slides with titles, key points, and pictures. And it does it in about a minute.

2083
02:40:32,048 --> 02:40:35,488
以前这需要你花整个下午去拖拽文本框。
Something that used to take you an afternoon of dragging text boxes around.

2084
02:40:35,694 --> 02:40:36,048
现在都不用了。
Gone.

2085
02:40:36,270 --> 02:40:38,048
只需点一下。这就是制作方法。
One click. Here's how you make one.

2086
02:40:38,208 --> 02:40:42,288
进入工作室面板，点击“创建幻灯片演示文稿”。
You go into the studio panel and you click create slide deck.

2087
02:40:42,448 --> 02:40:44,048
然后它会问你一个简单的问题。
Then it asks you a simple question.

2088
02:40:44,270 --> 02:40:46,928
你想要详细版幻灯片还是演讲者幻灯片？
Do you want a detailed deck or presenter slides?

2089
02:40:47,118 --> 02:40:49,408
这个选择很重要，让我来解释一下。
And this choice matters, so let me break it down.

2090
02:40:49,568 --> 02:40:57,316
详细版幻灯片在每张幻灯片上都包含更多文字。所以即使没有人现场讲解，它读起来也很通顺。
The detailed deck is packed with more text on every slide. So it reads well all on its own, even if nobody is standing there talking.

2091
02:40:57,518 --> 02:41:02,208
如果你打算通过邮件发送或者交给别人在空闲时间阅读，就选这个。
That's the one you want if you're going to send it in an email or hand it to someone to read on their own time.

2092
02:41:02,414 --> 02:41:03,488
它能自成体系。
It explains itself.

2093
02:41:03,726 --> 02:41:10,116
演讲者幻灯片则相反。它们简洁明了，只包含核心谈话点，大而清晰，不会太拥挤。
The presenter slides are the opposite. They're clean, just the key talking points, big and clear, not too crowded.

2094
02:41:10,318 --> 02:41:12,768
如果你是现场演示的人，就选这个。
That's the one you want when you're the one presenting live.

2095
02:41:12,928 --> 02:41:14,288
幻灯片是辅助你的。
The slides support you.

2096
02:41:14,414 --> 02:41:15,568
它们不需要承担所有的表达任务。
They don't do all the talking.

2097
02:41:15,790 --> 02:41:18,916
你用声音来填补空白，然后你可以对其进行自定义。
You fill in the gaps with your voice, then you get to customize it.

2098
02:41:19,088 --> 02:41:27,248
你可以设置语言、设定长度——比如简短的五页或更长的深度内容——并且可以添加一些风格说明，比如“保持简洁”
You can set the language, you can set the length, so a quick five slides or a longer deep one, and you can add a little style note, something like keep it simple

2099
02:41:27,408 --> 02:41:30,208
或者使用大地色系，或者让它看起来大胆且现代。
or use earth tones or make it feel bold and modern.

2100
02:41:30,318 --> 02:41:38,448
而且幻灯片上的图片是由 Google 的 Nano Banana Pro 生成的，这是他们最新的图像模型。所以它们看起来非常清晰，而不是那种廉价的剪贴画。
And the pictures it puts on the slides are made by Google's Nano Banana Pro, which is their newest image model. So they actually look sharp instead of cheesy clip art.

2101
02:41:38,608 --> 02:41:41,968
现在是这部分最棒的地方。假设第三页幻灯片做错了。
Now here's the part I love. Let's say slide three comes out wrong.

2102
02:41:42,128 --> 02:41:45,728
也许措辞不对，或者内容太杂乱。你不需要重做整个东西。
Maybe the wording is off or it's too busy. You don't redo the whole thing.

2103
02:41:45,808 --> 02:41:49,328
你只需输入「修复第三页幻灯片」，它就只会修改那一页。
You just type fix slide three and it fixes only that one.

2104
02:41:49,408 --> 02:41:55,888
或者要求「让第五页更短点」，它就会帮你删减。你甚至可以一次性排列几个这样的修改，然后让它一起完成。
Or make slide five shorter and it trims it. You can even line up a few of those edits at once and then let it redo them together.

2105
02:41:56,078 --> 02:41:58,288
所以你可以一页一页地把控进度。
So you stay in control slide by slide.

2106
02:41:58,446 --> 02:42:02,048
当你满意了，就可以把整个幻灯片演示文稿导出到 PowerPoint。
And when you're happy, you can export the whole deck to PowerPoint.

2107
02:42:02,222 --> 02:42:03,888
所以它不会被困在工具里面。
So it's not trapped inside the tool.

2108
02:42:04,048 --> 02:42:12,048
你把它拿出来，在 PowerPoint 里打开，随意修改你想改的地方就搞定了。Google 还表示以后可以直接在 Google Slides 里编辑，这会让操作变得更简单。
You pull it out, open it in PowerPoint, tweak whatever you want, and you're done. Google has also said editing straight in Google Slides is coming, which makes it even easier.

2109
02:42:12,128 --> 02:42:23,568
这就是我用的方法：我把那份包含 200 多个提示词的 PDF 导入，点击「创建幻灯片演示文稿」，选择「演讲者幻灯片」，然后它就会生成一个清晰的幻灯片，带你了解那个文件里的各种提示词类别。
So here's how I use it I take my 200 plus prompts, PDF, I hit create slide deck, I pick presenter slides, and out comes a clean deck that walks through the prompt categories in that file.

2110
02:42:23,790 --> 02:42:26,608
如果某页看起来不对，我就输入「修复第三页幻灯片」。
If one slide looks off, I type fix slide three.

2111
02:42:27,072 --> 02:42:27,872
搞定。
And it's sorted.

2112
02:42:28,046 --> 02:42:30,672
然后我把它导出到 PowerPoint，就可以分享了。
Then I export it to PowerPoint and it's ready to share.

2113
02:42:30,832 --> 02:42:40,192
还有一个小技巧：从同一个文件制作两个版本。一个是用于现场演讲的「演讲者幻灯片」，另一个是发给没能参加的人的「详细版幻灯片」。
And here's a little tip make two versions from the same file. One presenter deck for when you're talking live, and one detailed deck to send to people who missed it.

2114
02:42:40,398 --> 02:42:50,512
同一个文件，点两下，就能同时满足两种需求。这种操作能帮你省掉大半个下午的时间。好，下一个：音频概览。这是让这个工具出名的功能。
Same file, two clicks, and now you're covered both ways. That's the kind of thing that saves you a whole afternoon. Okay, next one audio overview. This is the one that made this tool famous.

2115
02:42:50,592 --> 02:42:52,192
一旦你试过之后，你就会明白为什么。
And once you try it, you'll get why.

2116
02:42:52,352 --> 02:42:59,152
音频概览能把你的文件变成播客，而不是机器人大声读你的笔记。而是真正的对话。
Audio overview turns your files into a podcast, not a robot reading your notes out loud. An actual conversation.

2117
02:42:59,406 --> 02:43:06,272
两个 AI 主持人用自然的嗓音来讨论你的素材。他们会开点玩笑，并互相补充内容。
Two AI hosts talking back and forth in natural voices about your material. They joke a little, they build on each other.

2118
02:43:06,446 --> 02:43:11,312
他们解释事情的方式就像两个聪明的朋友在为你拆解重点。听起来真的就像个节目。
They explain things like two smart friends breaking it down for you. It genuinely sounds like a show.

2119
02:43:11,534 --> 02:43:16,912
要制作一个，你只需在工作室里点击「音频概览」，然后等待几分钟让它生成。
To make one, you click audio overview in the studio and you wait a couple of minutes while it builds.

2120
02:43:17,072 --> 02:43:17,552
就这么简单。
That's it.

2121
02:43:17,712 --> 02:43:21,284
但你可以引导它，这才是厉害的地方。你可以选择格式。
But you can steer it, and this is where it gets good. You can pick the format.

2122
02:43:21,472 --> 02:43:23,632
有常规版，他们会过一遍所有内容。
There's the normal one where they walk through everything.

2123
02:43:23,854 --> 02:43:26,112
如果你只想快速了解一下，可以选择简略版。
There's a brief version if you just want the quick take.

2124
02:43:26,318 --> 02:43:33,792
还有辩论版，两个主持人会针对你的素材讨论不同的立场，这对于发现想法中的薄弱环节非常有用。
There's a debate version where the two hosts actually argue different sides of your material, which is amazing for seeing the weak spots in an idea.

2125
02:43:33,934 --> 02:43:37,712
还有评论版，他们会像评论家一样去剖析你的内容。
And there's a critique version where they pick your stuff apart, like reviewers.

2126
02:43:37,872 --> 02:43:45,540
你还可以设置语气和长度，并告诉它要重点关注什么。比如你可以说「侧重于初学者提示词」，它就会往那个方向靠。而且现在不再只有英文了。
You can also set the tone and the length and tell it what to focus on. So you can say focus on the beginner prompts and it leans that way. And it's not just English anymore.

2127
02:43:45,632 --> 02:43:54,020
它现在能用超过 80 种语言进行真正的对话。所以如果你用母语学习效果更好，这个门是敞开的。
It now does four proper conversations in over 80 languages. So if you learn better in your own language, that door is wide open.

2128
02:43:54,286 --> 02:43:56,912
不过，这个功能才是最让人惊艳的。
Here's the feature that blows people's minds, though.

2129
02:43:57,072 --> 02:43:58,052
你可以打断它。
You can interrupt it.

2130
02:43:58,272 --> 02:44:02,752
在播客播放时，你点击一个加入按钮，然后用你的声音提个问题。
While the podcast is playing, you hit a join button and you ask a question with your voice.

2131
02:44:02,958 --> 02:44:07,952
两位主持人会停下来，根据你的文件准确回答你的问题，然后继续节目。
The two hosts stop, answer your exact question using your file, and then carry right on with the show.

2132
02:44:08,110 --> 02:44:19,792
就像能在播客中举手，让他们真的回答你。通过我的提示词和加载的 PDF，我能让两名主持人讨论该文件中的最佳提示词。
It's like being able to raise your hand in the middle of a podcast and have them actually answer you. So with my prompts, PDF loaded, I get two hosts talking through the best prompts in that file.

2133
02:44:19,872 --> 02:44:24,912
每当我想要深入了解某一点时，我就可以插话提问，他们会直接从我的文件中提取内容进行讲解。
And anytime I want to go deeper on one, I jump in and ask, and they explain it pulling straight from my file.

2134
02:44:25,072 --> 02:44:34,112
这功能最出彩的地方在于，当你的手和眼睛正忙于散步、开车或洗碗时，你可以把文件变成一场节目。
Where this really shines is when your hands and eyes are busy on a walk, in the car, doing the dishes, you turn your files into a show

2135
02:44:34,286 --> 02:44:35,712
让你在移动中学习。
and you learn while you move.

2136
02:44:35,918 --> 02:44:42,912
这里有个技巧：如果你有一个包含很多部分的庞大文件，可以为每个部分制作独立的音频，即每个章节对应一个播客。
And here's a tip: if you've got a big file with lots of parts, make a separate audio for each part, one podcast per chapter.

2137
02:44:43,118 --> 02:44:46,512
这样你就拥有了一个完整的学习播放列表，而且全部都是基于一次上传生成的。
Now you've got a whole playlist to learn from, all built from one upload.

2138
02:44:46,702 --> 02:44:50,980
现在我们来聊聊视频概览，因为有时候你不想只是听。
Now let's talk video overview because sometimes you don't want to just listen.

2139
02:44:51,182 --> 02:44:56,512
你想看到它。如果说音频概览是播客，那么视频概览就是带旁白的幻灯片。
You want to see it. If audio overview is a podcast, video overview is a narrated slideshow.

2140
02:44:56,718 --> 02:45:02,912
屏幕上会出现幻灯片，并有语音引导你，在视觉效果切换的同时解释你的素材。
You get slides on the screen with a voice walking you through them, explaining your material as the visuals move along.

2141
02:45:03,072 --> 02:45:07,460
它提供同样有用的摘要，但现在你是通过观看来获取信息，这对很多人来说记忆效果更好。
It's the same helpful summary, but now you're watching it, which sticks better for a lot of people.

2142
02:45:07,694 --> 02:45:12,912
制作方法同样简单。在工作室中点击视频概览，它就会为你生成一个简短的视频演示。
You make it the same easy way. Click video overview in the studio and it builds you a little video presentation.

2143
02:45:13,198 --> 02:45:18,532
现在还有多种类型，让我来介绍一下。有一种是标准版，也就是带旁白的幻灯片。
And there's more than one kind now, so let me lay them out. There's the standard one, which is the narrated slideshow.

2144
02:45:18,702 --> 02:45:22,432
好消息是，即使在免费计划中也可以使用，每天最多支持三个。
And the good news is it works even on the free plan, up to three a day.

2145
02:45:22,512 --> 02:45:28,112
还有一个短版本，是一个 60 秒的竖屏片段，专为手机设计，非常适合随时随地快速回顾。
There's a short version, a 60-second vertical clip, built for your phone, perfect for a quick review on the go.

2146
02:45:28,272 --> 02:45:31,552
而在高级计划中，还有一个电影版，那是完全不同的层级。
And on the top plan, there's a cinematic one, which is a whole other level.

2147
02:45:31,726 --> 02:45:39,232
它不是静态幻灯片，而是带有流畅动态效果和丰富视觉效果的正式动画视频，能生动讲述你素材的故事。
Instead of static slides, it's a proper animated video with smooth motion and rich visuals that tell the story of your material.

2148
02:45:39,502 --> 02:45:44,352
Google 的模型会进行数百次细微的风格选择，让它看起来像一部真正的电影。
Google's model makes hundreds of little style choices to make it feel like a real film.

2149
02:45:44,590 --> 02:45:50,112
那个电影版目前仅支持英文，面向成年人，并且在高级层级中限制为每两天几次。
That cinematic one is English only for now, for grown-ups, and it's limited to a couple of days on the top tier.

2150
02:45:50,318 --> 02:45:54,432
无论选择哪种，你都可以添加引导说明，来引导视频朝着你想要的角度去呈现。
With any of them, you can add a steering note to point the video at the angle you want.

2151
02:45:54,592 --> 02:45:59,844
比如“为纯新手解释这个”，完成后，你可以播放、下载或通过链接分享它。
Like explain this for a total beginner, and when it's done, you can play it, download it, or share it with a link.

2152
02:46:00,112 --> 02:46:08,192
所以用我的提示词和 PDF 时，我点击视频概览，得到的不是播客，而是屏幕上直接展示这些提示词的演示视频。
So with my prompts, PDF, I hit video overview, and instead of a podcast, I get a walkthrough video of those prompts right there on screen.

2153
02:46:08,398 --> 02:46:14,432
如果我想在手机上稍后快速回顾，我就做那个短竖屏版。那么你什么时候会选择视频而不是音频呢？
If I want something quick to review on my phone later, I make the short vertical one. So when do you pick video over audio?

2154
02:46:14,638 --> 02:46:15,392
有个简单的规则。
Easy rule.

2155
02:46:15,552 --> 02:46:17,552
如果你需要腾出手来，就做音频。
If you need your eyes free, make audio.

2156
02:46:17,774 --> 02:46:24,352
如果看到文字和布局有助于理解，就做视频。你可以从同一个文件生成两种版本，保留你最终完成的那一个。
If seeing the words and the layout helps it click, make video. Try both from the same file and keep whichever one you actually finish.

2157
02:46:24,526 --> 02:46:25,792
那个才是最适合你的。
That's the one that's working for you.

2158
02:46:25,952 --> 02:46:26,272
明白了吗？
Alright?

2159
02:46:26,478 --> 02:46:30,032
下一个是大家经常忽略的功能，我想改变这一点。那就是思维导图。
This next one is the one people sleep on, and I want to fix that. The mind map.

2160
02:46:30,112 --> 02:46:37,712
思维导图会将你的整个文件转化为一张展示万物如何连接的图片。它会扫描所有素材并绘制出一张分支图。
A mind map takes your whole file and turns it into a picture of how everything connects. It scans all your material and lays out a branching map.

2161
02:46:37,902 --> 02:46:39,716
核心主旨位于中心位置。
The big main idea sits in the middle.

2162
02:46:39,952 --> 02:46:48,772
然后从中心延伸出分支，每个主题对应一个分支，更细小的细节则在这些分支上再分叉。这样你一眼就能看到素材的整体结构。
And then branches shoot off it, one for each topic, and smaller branches off those for the details. So in one glance, you see the whole shape of your material.

2163
02:46:49,102 --> 02:46:55,876
你在工作室里点击「思维导图」即可生成。而且它最特别的一点是：它不是一张只能盯着看的平面图。
You make it by clicking mind map in the studio. And here's the thing that makes it special. It's not a flat picture you just stare at.

2164
02:46:56,032 --> 02:47:00,032
它是可以点击的。你点击一个分支，它就会展开并显示底层的详细内容。
It's clickable. You tap a branch and it opens up and shows you what's underneath.

2165
02:47:00,192 --> 02:47:02,112
你可以不断点击，深入探索。
You keep tapping and you keep going deeper.

2166
02:47:02,254 --> 02:47:06,832
你甚至可以点击地图上的某个主题进行提问，它会直接从你的源文件中提取答案。
And you can even click a topic on the map and ask about it, and it will pull the answer straight from your sources.

2167
02:47:07,072 --> 02:47:16,112
为什么我这么喜欢这个？因为它理解庞杂内容最快的方法。与其去从头到尾读 40 页纸，不如看一眼地图，你就知道这些内容是怎么串联起来的。
Why do I love this so much? Because it's the fastest way to understand something big. Instead of reading 40 pages front to back, you look at one map and go, oh, that's how this all fits together.

2168
02:47:16,272 --> 02:47:18,752
在你去看具体的细节之前，先看到整片森林。
You see the whole forest before you go looking at the trees.

2169
02:47:18,926 --> 02:47:26,272
它也非常适合发现漏洞。当所有内容都铺开时，你会注意到那些分支很薄、或者你还没真正理解的部分。
It's also brilliant for spotting gaps. When you see it all laid out, you notice the branch that's thin, the part you don't actually understand yet.

2170
02:47:26,638 --> 02:47:34,864
所以当我对我的提示词 PDF 运行「思维导图」时，它会按主题对提示词进行分组，并展示不同类型之间是如何关联的。
So when I run Mind Map on my prompts PDF, it groups the prompts by theme and shows me how the different types connect to each other.

2171
02:47:35,086 --> 02:47:41,604
大约 10 秒钟内，我就能看到这个文件的整体布局，而不需要按顺序读过每一页。这是我的核心秘诀：
In about 10 seconds, I can see the whole layout of that file without reading a single page in order. And here's my real tip.

2172
02:47:41,904 --> 02:47:46,784
在做任何事情之前，先制作思维导图。用它来掌握全局情况。
Make the mind map first before anything else. Use it to get the lay of the land.

2173
02:47:46,944 --> 02:47:50,224
然后再去制作你的报告、音频或 Slides。
Then go make your report or your audio or your slides.

2174
02:47:50,384 --> 02:47:59,824
既然你已经真正理解了正在处理内容的结构，其他事情就变得简单多了。如果你是视觉型的人，单是这个工具就非常值得。好，接下来看「报告」。
Now that you actually understand the shape of what you're working with, it makes everything else easier. If you're a visual person, this tool alone is worth the whole thing. Okay, reports.

2175
02:48:00,014 --> 02:48:01,104
这是主力工具。
This is the workhorse.

2176
02:48:01,424 --> 02:48:07,744
「报告」功能会将你的源文件转化为整洁的文字文档。是真正实用且有条理的写作。
Reports takes your sources and turns them into clean written documents. Real, useful, organized writing.

2177
02:48:07,904 --> 02:48:12,064
你在工作室里点击「报告」，就会看到几个现成的选项供你选择。
You click reports in the studio and you get a few ready-made options to pick from.

2178
02:48:12,334 --> 02:48:19,104
这里有「简报文档」，它会把源文件中的所有要点和重要引用提取到一个整洁的概览中。
There's the briefing doc which pulls all the key points and important quotes from your files into one tidy overview.

2179
02:48:19,278 --> 02:48:22,464
当你需要快速掌握大意或让别人快速了解情况时，这个非常好用。
Great when you need to get the gist fast or catch someone else up.

2180
02:48:22,702 --> 02:48:24,864
还有「学习指南」，这个功能内容很丰富。
There's the study guide, and this one is loaded.

2181
02:48:25,038 --> 02:48:35,184
它不只是总结，还包含测验、建议的作文题目和核心术语词汇表。所以它基本上就是一个现成的复习包。
It doesn't just summarize, it comes with a quiz, suggested essay questions, and a glossary of the key terms. So it's basically a ready-made revision pack.

2182
02:48:35,374 --> 02:48:43,264
如果你想把素材变成文章，可以选择「博客文章」格式；还有「常见问题解答」风格，能把你的内容转化成简单的问答。
There's a blog post format if you want your material shaped into an article, and there's an FAQ style too, which turns your stuff into simple questions and answers.

2183
02:48:43,470 --> 02:48:45,424
但这里有一个大多数人忽略的巧妙之处。
But here's the clever bit that most people miss.

2184
02:48:45,710 --> 02:48:53,252
「报告」不仅提供这些默认选项，它还会阅读你的源文件，并推荐真正契合你主题的报告类型。
Reports doesn't only give you those default options, it reads your sources and suggests report types that actually fit your topic.

2185
02:48:53,454 --> 02:49:01,984
所以健康领域的 Notebook 和营销领域的 Notebook 不会得到相同的选择。它会根据你上传的内容，提供针对该主题定制的格式。
So a health notebook and a marketing notebook won't get the same choices. It looks at what you uploaded and offers formats built for that subject.

2186
02:49:02,144 --> 02:49:05,424
就像它在思考哪些内容对你的素材真正有用。
It's like it thinks about what would actually be useful for your material.

2187
02:49:05,646 --> 02:49:07,940
如果你想要完全掌控，可以选择「自定义」。
And if you want full control, you can go custom.

2188
02:49:08,110 --> 02:49:17,024
你可以设定结构、风格、语气，并从 80 多种语言中选择一种。无论你需要正式还是随意，长篇大论还是简明扼要，都能做到。
You set the structure, you set the style, you set the tone, and you set the language from over 80 of them. So you can make it formal or casual, short or detailed, however you need it.

2189
02:49:17,104 --> 02:49:20,784
而且和这里的其他功能一样，每一个点都会链接回它最初的出处。
And like everything else in here, every point links back to the source it came from.

2190
02:49:20,942 --> 02:49:29,540
所以你可以随时核实。当我针对提示词 PDF 点击「报告」并选择「简报文档」时，它会把最优质的提示词和创意提取到一份整洁的文稿中，我可以在一分钟内扫完。
So you can always check it. So I hit reports on my prompts PDF, pick briefing doc and it pulls the best prompts and ideas into one clean write-up I can skim in a minute.

2191
02:49:29,664 --> 02:49:39,664
或者我选学习指南，这样我就能从同一个文件中获得测验和核心术语来测试自己。只需点一下，我那乱七八糟的 PDF 就变成了真正可以学习或分享的内容。
Or I pick study guide, and now I've got a quiz and key terms to test myself with from the same file. One click and my messy PDF becomes something I can actually learn from or share.

2192
02:49:39,886 --> 02:49:42,340
这是当你需要把内容落到纸面上时会用的选项。
This is the one I'd use when you need something on paper.

2193
02:49:42,544 --> 02:49:46,064
参考文档、学习包，或者文章的初稿。
A reference doc, a study pack, a first draft of an article.

2194
02:49:46,224 --> 02:49:49,732
它能把原始素材处理成整洁且实用的形式。
It takes the raw material and gives it a clean, usable shape.

2195
02:49:50,062 --> 02:49:55,824
在教大家如何组合这些工具之前，我先给几个小贴士，能让每一个结果都变得更好。
Before I show you how to stack these together, let me give you a few quick tips that make every one of these come out better.

2196
02:49:56,014 --> 02:49:59,024
这些细节很小，但影响很大，而且大多数人都会忽略它们。
They're small, but they make a big difference, and most people skip them.

2197
02:49:59,184 --> 02:50:01,344
提示一，先清理你的源文件。
Tip one, clean up your sources first.

2198
02:50:01,550 --> 02:50:03,984
工作室的质量取决于你喂给它的内容。
The studio is only as good as what you feed it.

2199
02:50:04,144 --> 02:50:07,744
如果你扔进去一个乱七八糟、没写完的文件，得到的结果也会很乱。
If you dump in a messy, half-finished file, you get a messy result back.

2200
02:50:07,918 --> 02:50:11,664
如果你提供一个清晰、有重点的文件，就能得到非常精准的内容。
If you drop in a clear, focused file, you get something sharp.

2201
02:50:11,822 --> 02:50:14,544
所以给它高质量的素材，它就会给你更好的回报。
So give it good material to work with and it rewards you.

2202
02:50:14,704 --> 02:50:17,252
提示二，每次都要使用引导说明。
Tip two, use the steering note every single time.

2203
02:50:17,424 --> 02:50:21,424
这里几乎每个工具都在生成内容前都允许你添加一点指令。
Almost every tool in here lets you add a little instruction before it builds.

2204
02:50:21,646 --> 02:50:22,544
别让它空白。
Don't leave it blank.

2205
02:50:22,766 --> 02:50:25,156
告诉它这是给谁看的，以及要重点关注什么。
Tell it who this is for and what to focus on.

2206
02:50:25,344 --> 02:50:27,492
比如，说：这是给纯小白看的。
Say, make this for a total beginner.

2207
02:50:27,664 --> 02:50:29,584
或者说：重点放在 SEO 提示词上。
Say focus on the SEO prompts.

2208
02:50:29,744 --> 02:50:31,264
或者说：保持简洁明了。
Say keep it short and simple.

2209
02:50:31,502 --> 02:50:35,424
你告诉它的信息越多，生成的内容就越接近你脑海中的构思。
The more you tell it, the closer it lands to what you actually pictured in your head.

2210
02:50:35,584 --> 02:50:38,464
提示三，多做几个版本。
Tip three, make more than one version.

2211
02:50:38,704 --> 02:50:47,264
这个工具很快而且免费试用，所以别满足于它给你的第一个结果。做一个简短版，做一个长篇版。做一个给自己用的，再做一个分享用的。
This tool is fast and it's free to try, so don't settle for the first thing it hands you. Make a short version and a long one. Make one for yourself and one to share.

2212
02:50:47,424 --> 02:50:49,824
做一个用通俗语言表达的，再做一个包含更多细节的。
Make one in plain words and one with more detail.

2213
02:50:50,062 --> 02:50:51,024
然后保留最好的那个。
Then keep the best.

2214
