这是你的下一步，也是为你制定计划最快的方法。
That's your next step, and it's the fastest way to get a plan made for you.

2253
02:53:36,430 --> 02:53:40,400
当你开始使用这些工作室工具时，你可能会遇到一些小问题。
And once you start playing with these studio tools, you're going to run into little questions.

2254
02:53:40,622 --> 02:53:41,988
“这里我该用什么格式？”
Which format should I use here?

2255
02:53:42,222 --> 02:53:43,600
“为什么我的卡片组变成了这样？”
Why did my deck come out like that?

2256
02:53:43,822 --> 02:53:45,280
“我怎么能让整个过程变快点？”
How do I make this whole thing faster?

2257
02:53:45,486 --> 02:53:48,836
这正是我的社区 AI Profit Boardroom 的作用所在。
That's exactly what my community, the AI Profit Boardroom, is for.

2258
02:53:49,040 --> 02:53:53,040
在里面，你可以看到我今天展示的那些工具的完整操作演示。
Inside, you get full walkthroughs of the exact tools I showed you today.

2259
02:53:53,200 --> 02:53:58,640
我们有实时的教练通话，你可以共享屏幕，并实时向我咨询你自己的设置问题。
We run live coaching calls where you can share your screen and ask me about your own setup in real time.

2260
02:53:58,926 --> 02:54:03,840
还有路线图会告诉你第一步、第二步和第三步该做什么，让你永远不会对着空白屏幕发愁。
There are roadmaps that tell you what to do first, second, and third, so you're never staring at a blank screen.

2261
02:54:03,982 --> 02:54:09,040
而且还有整套现成的提示词和教程，让你永远不需要从零开始。
And there's a whole stack of prompts and tutorials ready to go, so you're never starting from zero.

2262
02:54:09,294 --> 02:54:14,480
我们现在有超过 4000 名成员，大家都在一起学习这些内容，并互相帮助提高效率。
We're over 4,000 members strong now, all learning this stuff together and helping each other move faster.

2263
02:54:14,734 --> 02:54:18,948
如果这正是你需要的，欢迎加入我们：aiprofitboardroom.com。
If that sounds like what you need, come join us at aiprofitboardroom.com.

2264
02:54:19,280 --> 02:54:21,440
还剩四个。好，我们继续。
Four left. Alright, let's keep it going.

2265
02:54:21,680 --> 02:54:28,080
接下来是抽认卡。抽认卡就在你 Notebook 的工作室面板里。
Next up on our list, flashcards. So flashcards live inside the studio panel of your notebook.

2266
02:54:28,238 --> 02:54:35,108
在所有的功能中，这是最容易让人爱上的工具之一，因为它能做我们都希望有更多时间去做的事情。
And out of everything in here, this is one of the simplest tools to fall in love with because it does something we all wish we had more time to do.

2267
02:54:35,280 --> 02:54:39,920
它能在几秒钟内，无需你动手操作，就把你的素材变成学习卡片。
It turns your material into study cards for you in a few seconds without you lifting a finger.

2268
02:54:40,142 --> 02:54:42,800
但这里有一个让它们真正值得使用的原因。
But here's the part that actually makes them worth using.

2269
02:54:43,054 --> 02:54:48,000
Notebook LM 直接根据你上传的源文件来生成抽认卡。
Notebook LM builds the flashcards straight from the sources you upload.

2270
02:54:48,174 --> 02:54:51,920
它不是从模型大脑里那些泛泛而谈的内容中提取信息。
It's not pulling from some generic version of the topic that lives in the model's head.

2271
02:54:52,014 --> 02:54:54,640
它是从你放在它面前的特定文档中提取内容。
It's pulling from the exact document you put in front of it.

2272
02:54:54,862 --> 02:55:03,040
所以，如果你放入自己的笔记、长篇 PDF、培训文档或整本指南，生成的卡片就是基于这些内容的
So if you drop in your own notes, a long PDF, a training doc, or a whole guide, the cards you get back are grounded in that material

2273
02:55:03,214 --> 02:55:05,280
而不会包含其他任何信息。那么，为什么这很重要呢？
and nothing else. Now, why does that matter so much?

2274
02:55:05,518 --> 02:55:08,000
想想你在网上能找到的普通抽认卡。
Think about a normal set of flashcards you'd find online.

2275
02:55:08,270 --> 02:55:14,480
它们复习的是任何版本的知识点。有些可能是对的，但很大一部分内容可能和你真正需要知道的内容毫无关系。
They review any old version of a subject. Some of it might be right, but a chunk of it might have nothing to do with what you actually need to know.

2276
02:55:14,640 --> 02:55:17,040
有了 Notebook LM，这个问题就解决了。
With Notebook LM, that problem goes away.

2277
02:55:17,326 --> 02:55:25,600
这些卡片会针对你的素材、笔记和教学大纲进行测验，这样你就不会浪费时间去记忆那些虽然正确但与你主题完全无关的内容了。
The cards quiz you on your material, your notes, your syllabus, so you're never wasting time memorizing stuff that's correct, but completely off topic for you.

2278
02:55:25,774 --> 02:55:27,600
所有内容都关联到你上传的内容上。
Everything ties back to what you uploaded.

2279
02:55:27,760 --> 02:55:29,840
使用它们非常简单。
Using them is about as simple as it gets.

2280
02:55:30,062 --> 02:55:35,280
你打开工作室面板，点击抽认卡板块，它就会在几秒钟内为你生成一套卡片。
You open the studio panel, you click the flashcards tile, and it generates a deck for you in seconds.

2281
02:55:35,440 --> 02:55:38,800
卡片正面会出现一个问题，你思考一下答案。
A question shows up on the front of the card, you think about your answer.

2282
02:55:39,022 --> 02:55:41,668
然后点击翻转卡片，看看你答对没。
Then you click to flip the card and see if you got it right.

2283
02:55:41,840 --> 02:55:50,800
当你生成一组卡片时，它会以简洁的全屏视图打开。说实话，感觉和很多你常用的学习应用很像。所以没什么学习门槛，直接开始翻牌就行。
When you generate a set, it opens up in a clean full screen view. Honestly, it feels a lot like the study apps you might already know. So there's no learning curve, you just start flipping.

2284
02:55:51,168 --> 02:55:55,328
而且你不需要被动接受它给你的内容。在它构建任何东西之前，你可以先进行引导。
And you don't have to take whatever it hands you. You can guide it before it builds anything.

2285
02:55:55,534 --> 02:55:57,568
只需先点击那个小铅笔图标。
Just click the little pencil icon first.

2286
02:55:57,774 --> 02:56:01,728
从那里你可以设置卡片数量，少一点、标准或者多一些。
From there you can set the number of cards, fewer, standard, or more.

2287
02:56:01,902 --> 02:56:05,168
你还可以设置难度，简单、中等或困难。
You can set the difficulty, easy, medium, or hard.

2288
02:56:05,248 --> 02:56:09,060
而且你可以让它针对一个特定主题，而不是整篇文档。
And you can point it at one specific topic instead of the whole document.

2289
02:56:09,326 --> 02:56:18,020
所以与其得到一堆随机的卡片，你可以告诉它制作一个更大的卡组，保留较难的问题，并且只专注于你薄弱的一个章节或一个科目。
So instead of a random pile of cards, you could tell it to make a bigger deck, keep the questions on the hard side, and focus only on one chapter or one subject you're weak on.

2290
02:56:18,208 --> 02:56:24,048
你甚至可以用纯文本指令来引导它，比如要求把卡片的正面写短一点，这样一眼就能记住。
You can even guide it with a plain text instruction, like asking for shorter fronts on the cards so they're easier to memorize at a glance.

2291
02:56:24,208 --> 02:56:32,208
假设你上传了一份很长的培训文档，系统会为你构建一个紧凑的学习卡组，只包含对你重要的部分，并符合你想要的难度。
Say you uploaded a long training doc, You'd get a tight study deck built around just the parts that matter to you at the exact difficulty you want.

2292
02:56:32,368 --> 02:56:41,008
还有个在 2026 年推出的不错的功能。在很长一段时间里，卡片一旦生成就被锁定。你没法修改错误的答案或者添加缺失的内容。
And here's a nice upgrade that landed in 2026. For a long time, the cards were locked once they were made. You couldn't fix a wrong answer or add one that was missing.

2293
02:56:41,168 --> 02:56:41,888
现在情况变了。
That changed.

2294
02:56:42,094 --> 02:56:51,328
现在的闪卡是完全可编辑的。你可以重写问题，微调不太准确的答案，删除不需要的卡片，甚至从头开始制作全新的卡片。
Now the flash cards are fully editable. You can rewrite a question, tweak an answer that isn't quite right, delete the cards you don't need, and even build brand new cards from scratch.

2295
02:56:51,566 --> 02:56:55,808
所以如果 AI 漏掉了什么，你不用受困。你只需自己修正它并继续下去。
So if the AI misses something, you're not stuck. You just fix it yourself and keep going.

2296
02:56:55,950 --> 02:57:00,848
接下来这个功能真正让它从一个简单的演示变成了一个严肃的学习工具。
Now here's the feature that really turns this from a quick demo into a serious study tool.

2297
02:57:01,102 --> 02:57:02,128
卡组会记住你的进度。
The deck remembers you.

2298
02:57:02,318 --> 02:57:05,284
在你练习的过程中，你可以把卡片分类为「掌握了」和「没掌握」。
As you go through, you sort your cards into got it and missed it.

2299
02:57:05,422 --> 02:57:07,408
它会在不同会话之间保存这种分类。
And it saves that sort between sessions.

2300
02:57:07,630 --> 02:57:15,888
所以如果你周一练过这些卡片，周三再回来时，它会直接从你没掌握的那些开始，而不是那些你已经烂熟于心的内容。
So if you work through your cards on Monday and come back on Wednesday, it picks up right where you left off on the ones you missed, not the ones you already knew cold.

2301
02:57:16,048 --> 02:57:21,968
这基本上就是后台在为你自动处理间隔重复。你不需要手动去追踪你的薄弱点。
That's basically spaced repetition doing the heavy lifting for you in the background. You don't have to track your weak spots by hand.

2302
02:57:22,190 --> 02:57:26,848
这个工具会默默地不断推送那些你一直做错的卡片，直到你彻底掌握为止。
The tool just quietly keeps serving you the cards you keep getting wrong until they finally stick.

2303
02:57:27,054 --> 02:57:28,688
而且它之后变得更加智能了。
And it got even smarter after that.

2304
02:57:28,878 --> 02:57:34,848
一旦你完成一组练习，它会给你一个快速的主题摘要，让你看到自己的水平。它还会建议你接下来该学什么。
Once you run through a set, it gives you a quick topic summary so you can see where you stand. It suggests what you should study next.

2305
02:57:34,928 --> 02:57:38,528
还有一个重新生成按钮，可以直接针对你的薄弱点进行强化。
And there's a regenerate button that drills straight into your weak spots.

2306
02:57:38,670 --> 02:57:41,488
所以你不需要去猜该复习什么，工具会直接指引你。
So instead of guessing what to review, the tool points you at it.

2307
02:57:41,648 --> 02:57:51,168
它在移动端 App 上也可用，这意味着你可以在排队或乘公交时翻几张卡片。它是为碎片化学习设计的，而不只是为了长时间坐下来学习。
It also works on the mobile app, which means you can review a few cards while you're waiting in line or riding the bus. It's built for short bursts, not just long sit-down sessions.

2308
02:57:51,374 --> 02:57:59,408
还有一点，因为现在可以编辑了，它们也很容易分享。所以如果你是和别人一起学习，或者你做了一个很棒的卡组想分享出去，你可以这样做。
One more thing, because they're editable now, they're also easy to share. So if you're studying with someone else or you made a great deck you want to pass along, you can.

2309
02:57:59,568 --> 02:58:07,248
让我把这个如何融入到真实日常中的全貌描绘出来，因为只有这样你才能真正领会它的价值。想象一下你有大量素材需要消化。
Let me paint the full picture of how this fits into a real routine because that's when it clicks. Imagine you've got a big set of material to get through.

2310
02:58:07,408 --> 02:58:11,332
在第一天，你上传它，生成一个卡组，并完成全部内容。
On day one, you upload it, generate a deck, and run through all of it.

2311
02:58:11,488 --> 02:58:13,380
标记出你掌握的内容和还没掌握的内容。
You mark what you knew and what you didn't.

2312
02:58:13,568 --> 02:58:18,724
到了第二天，打开同一个 NotebookLM，内容已经分类好了，你可以直接去复习错过的抽认卡。
On day two, you open the same notebook and it's already sorted, you go straight to the cards you missed.

2313
02:58:18,958 --> 02:58:28,608
到了第三天，查看主题摘要，看看哪些领域还不稳，然后点击重新生成来专项练习。你不需要重构任何东西，也不需要在白板上制定学习计划。
On day three, you check the topic summary, see which area is still shaky, and hit regenerate to drill just that. You're not rebuilding anything. You're not making a study plan on a whiteboard.

2314
02:58:28,782 --> 02:58:35,408
工具在处理复习的结构，而你只需要出现并进行练习，而且每一张抽认卡，每一个步骤，
The tool is handling the structure of your review while you just show up and do the reps, and every single card, every step of the way,

2315
02:58:35,568 --> 02:58:40,528
都是从你自己上传的素材中提取的，所以你永远不会偏离到那些你不需要的内容上。
is pulled from your own uploaded material so you never drift off into stuff you don't actually need.

2316
02:58:40,814 --> 02:58:46,288
在继续之前，关于抽认卡我给你个小建议，因为这个技巧真的很有用。
Let me give you a quick piece of advice on flashcards before we move on, because this one tip makes a real difference.

2317
02:58:46,478 --> 02:58:53,808
只保留你真正想要测试的源文件。在工作室里，你可以临时勾选或取消勾选你的源文件。
Only keep the sources selected that you actually want tested. Inside the studio, you can temporarily check and uncheck your sources.

2318
02:58:54,030 --> 02:58:57,156
这样，卡片组就只会从你目前关心的内容中构建出来。
So the deck is built only from the material you care about right now.

2319
02:58:57,390 --> 02:59:06,084
如果你保留一大堆多余的内容，抽认卡可能会变得模糊且偏离主题。所以先精简一下。还有一点需要知道的是，它没有原生的导出按钮。
If you leave a bunch of extra stuff checked, the cards can get muddy and off topic. So trim it down first. And one thing to know going in, there's no native export button.

2320
02:59:06,222 --> 02:59:08,928
你不能一键将抽认卡推送到另一个应用中。
You can't push the deck straight into another app with one click.

2321
02:59:09,134 --> 02:59:17,728
所以如果你想把抽认卡保存在别的地方，比如在 Anki 里，你需要把问题和答案复制到电子表格中并从那里导入，或者直接截个图。
So if you want to keep the cards somewhere else, like in Anki, you'll need to copy the questions and answers out into a spreadsheet and import them from there, or just grab a quick screenshot.

2322
02:59:17,888 --> 02:59:21,168
这是一个小小的限制，但在构建庞大的抽认卡之前值得了解一下。
It's a small catch, but worth knowing before you build a huge deck.

2323
02:59:21,248 --> 02:59:27,888
现在，抽认卡对于将事实推入你的记忆非常棒，但记住某件事和真正能够运用它是两回事。
Now, flashcards are great for pushing facts into your memory, but memorizing something and actually being able to use it are two different things.

2324
02:59:28,048 --> 02:59:32,368
所以如果你想测试这些信息是否真的扎根了，这就是下一个工具派上用场的地方。
So if you want to test whether the information really stuck, that's where the next tool comes in.

2325
02:59:32,528 --> 02:59:33,008
就是测验。
The quiz.

2326
02:59:33,166 --> 02:59:38,368
测验的工作原理和抽认卡很像，但你不是在翻转卡片，而是在回答真实的问题。
The quiz works a lot like the flashcards, but instead of flipping cards, you're answering real questions.

2327
02:59:38,638 --> 02:59:43,968
你前往工作室面板，点击测验，它会直接从你的源文件中构建出一套问题。
You head to the studio panel, click quiz, and it builds a set of questions straight from your sources.

2328
02:59:44,206 --> 02:59:46,528
你选择答案，它会告诉你你的表现如何。
You pick your answer and it tells you how you did.

2329
02:59:46,702 --> 02:59:49,808
完成之后，你会得到一个分数和整套题目的概览。
When you finish, you get a score and an overview of the whole set.

2330
02:59:49,968 --> 02:59:55,088
之后你可以回去复习问题，或者重新运行测验看看自己有没有进步。
And you can go back and review the questions afterward or run the quiz again to see if you've improved.

2331
02:59:55,248 --> 02:59:59,088
所以它不是一次性的，而是一个你可以反复练习的循环。
So it's not just a one and done thing, it's a loop you can keep coming back to.

2332
02:59:59,310 --> 03:00:03,168
测验真正的强大之处在于它测试你的理解力，而不只是记忆力。
The real strength of the quiz is that it tests your understanding, not just your memory.

2333
03:00:03,406 --> 03:00:05,488
抽认卡检查你是否记得某个事实。
Flashcards check whether you remember a fact.

2334
03:00:05,742 --> 03:00:07,716
好的测验则检查你是否真的懂了。
A good quiz checks whether you actually get it.

2335
03:00:07,886 --> 03:00:15,972
就像抽认卡一样，你可以在生成前对其进行塑造。你可以设置问题的数量、难度以及你想让它重点关注的主题。
And just like the flashcards, you can shape it before you generate. You can set the number of questions, the difficulty, and the topic you want it to focus on.

2336
03:00:16,238 --> 03:00:26,128
但当你为测验编写自定义指令时，它的潜力才真正被释放出来。而这正是大多数人错失价值的地方，因为他们只是点击生成并接受任何出来的结果。
But the quiz really opens up when you write a custom instruction for it. And this is where most people leave value on the table because they just click generate and take whatever comes out.

2337
03:00:26,478 --> 03:00:29,872
让我给你举几个你可以输入的实际例子。
Let me give you a couple of real examples of the kind of thing you can type instead.

2338
03:00:30,158 --> 03:00:38,432
最简单的版本就像这样：要求它生成一个包含 20 个问题、涵盖你上传源文件中特定章节或单元的难题测验。
The simplest version is something like this. Ask it to generate a hard quiz with 20 questions covering one specific chapter or unit from your uploaded sources.

2339
03:00:38,638 --> 03:00:43,780
仅仅这点引导就能给你提供重点，让你得到一套有挑战性的题目，而不是随机抓取的题库。
Just that little bit of direction gives you a focus, challenging set instead of a random grab bag.

2340
03:00:43,872 --> 03:00:45,312
但你还可以深入得多。
But you can go a lot deeper.

2341
03:00:45,472 --> 03:00:48,352
你可以要求它构建一个包含三个层级的 20 道题测验。
You could ask it to build a 20 question quiz in three tiers.

2342
03:00:48,558 --> 03:00:53,232
第一层，前几道题测试基础记忆，也就是关键事实和定义。
Tier one, the first several questions tests basic recall, the key facts and definitions.

2343
03:00:53,392 --> 03:00:57,952
第二层，中间部分测试你是否理解这些概念之间的联系和对比。
Tier two, the middle chunk tests whether you understand how the ideas connect and compare.

2344
03:00:58,126 --> 03:01:04,112
第三层，最后几题测试你是否能将所学内容应用到新情况中。
And tier three, the last few tests whether you can actually apply what you've learned to a new situation.

2345
03:01:04,366 --> 03:01:09,792
此外，你还可以要求它为每个问题提供正确答案和一句解释。
On top of that, you tell it to include the correct answer and a one sentence explanation for each question.

2346
03:01:09,952 --> 03:01:16,832
这样你就不仅仅得到了一个测验，而是拥有了一个从基础记忆到真正实用的理解的完整学习工具。
Now you don't just have a quiz, you've got a proper study tool that walks you from basic memory all the way up to real usable understanding.

2347
03:01:17,134 --> 03:01:20,196
而且这个测验能完美配合我之前提到的智能功能。
And the quiz plays beautifully with the smart features I mentioned earlier.

2348
03:01:20,432 --> 03:01:23,952
完成一轮后，它会总结出你遇到的难题。
After a round, it summarizes the topics you struggled with.

2349
03:01:24,142 --> 03:01:26,272
这样你的下一步行动就能非常精准。
So your next move can be really targeted.

2350
03:01:26,382 --> 03:01:35,792
你可以让它生成一个只针对刚才标记为需要更多练习的概念的新测验，提高难度，然后对比你这一轮的表现。
You could tell it to generate a fresh quiz focused only on the concepts it just flagged as needing more practice, crank the difficulty up, and then compare your performance to the last round.

2351
03:01:35,952 --> 03:01:42,992
这建立了一个闭环反馈：你做测验，它显示你的短板，你攻克这些短板，并看着它们随着时间的推移而减少。
That creates a closed feedback loop. You quiz, it shows you your gaps, you drill the gaps, and you watch them close over time.

2352
03:01:43,214 --> 03:01:47,524
这是一种非常强大的学习方式，而且所有内容都基于你自己的素材。
That's a genuinely powerful way to learn, and it's all grounded in your own material.

2353
03:01:47,854 --> 03:01:52,672
还有一个在生成测验之前的聪明技巧，那就是使用对话功能。
There's also a smart trick that happens before you even generate the quiz, and that's using the chat.

2354
03:01:52,846 --> 03:02:01,792
在构建任何东西之前，你可以通过对话与你的源文件交流，让它提取主要主题，甚至可以让它扮演一位严厉的教授来考查你对这些内容的掌握情况。
Before you build anything, you can talk to your sources in the chat and ask it to pull out the main themes or even tell it to act like a strict professor grilling you on the material.

2355
03:02:02,062 --> 03:02:10,432
对话功能可以承担这样的角色或语气，这样你可以把它变成一个严厉的学习伙伴，它会质疑你的答案并指出你思考中的模糊之处。
The chat can take on a role or a voice like that, so you can turn it into a tough study partner that pushes back on your answers and points out where your thinking is fuzzy.

2356
03:02:10,512 --> 03:02:18,912
这少量的预处理能帮你确定哪些内容值得测验。这样生成的测验就会更精准，直击你真正不确定的部分。
That little bit of pre-work helps you figure out what's worth quizzing on in the first place. So your quiz comes out sharper and hits the stuff you're actually unsure about.

2357
03:02:19,214 --> 03:02:21,312
想想这节省了多少时间。
And think about how much time this collapses.

2358
03:02:21,486 --> 03:02:32,068
通常情况下，制作一个好的练习测验意味着要阅读所有内容、判断重点、编写问题、设计合理的干扰项，然后再写出每个答案为什么正确。
Normally, building a good practice quiz means reading everything, deciding what's important, writing the questions, writing plausible wrong answers, and then writing out why each answer is right.

2359
03:02:32,302 --> 03:02:34,980
那得花好几个小时。而且老实说，大多数人根本不会这么做。
That's hours of work. And honestly, most people never do it.

2360
03:02:35,152 --> 03:02:36,900
他们只是重读笔记然后祈祷能记住。
They just reread their notes and hope.

2361
03:02:37,232 --> 03:02:46,112
在这里，你只需几秒钟就能得到所有这些内容，而且是根据你的特定素材和你选择的难度量身定制的。真正测试自己的门槛几乎消失了。
Here, you get all of that in a few seconds, tailored to your exact material at whatever difficulty you choose. The barrier to actually testing yourself just about disappears.

2362
03:02:46,222 --> 03:02:54,272
而自我测试是让信息入脑最有效的方法之一。就像抽认卡一样，测验也可以在手机上运行，所以你可以随时随地进行测试。
And testing yourself is one of the most proven ways to make information stick. And like the flashcards, the quiz works on mobile too, so you can test yourself anywhere.

2363
03:02:54,432 --> 03:02:56,432
关于测验，我的建议简单明了。
My advice on the quiz is short and simple.

2364
03:02:56,622 --> 03:02:58,912
不要只是点击生成就满足于默认结果。
Don't just hit generate and settle for the default.

2365
03:02:59,072 --> 03:03:03,312
花 10 秒钟写一个自定义指令，就像我刚才描述的那个分层式的。
Spend 10 seconds writing a custom instruction like the tiered one I described.

2366
03:03:03,472 --> 03:03:08,192
这一个小小的步骤就是基础测验和真正能教给你东西的测验之间的区别。
That one small step is the difference between a basic quiz and one that actually teaches you something.

2367
03:03:08,352 --> 03:03:14,992
如果你有一大堆源文件，先在对话中挖掘一下主题。另外提醒一下，和抽认卡一样，目前还没有干净的导出功能。
Do a little theme digging in the chat first if you've got a big set of sources. And a quick heads up, same as the flashcards, there's no clean export.

2368
03:03:15,152 --> 03:03:20,900
所以任何你想留到以后用的内容都截图保存。好吗？所以前两个工具都是关于学习和记忆的。
So screenshot anything you want to keep for later. Okay? So those first two tools are all about studying and remembering.

2369
03:03:21,102 --> 03:03:23,072
下一个工具的功能完全不同。
This next one does a completely different job.

2370
03:03:23,278 --> 03:03:26,352
它不是为了记忆，而是为了组织和对比。
It's not about memorizing, it's about organizing and comparing.

2371
03:03:26,512 --> 03:03:27,872
这是数据表。
This is the data table.

2372
03:03:28,078 --> 03:03:34,672
数据表能把杂乱、冗长的信息转化成整洁、有结构的表格。
The data table takes messy, wordy information and turns it into a clean, structured table.

2373
03:03:34,894 --> 03:03:44,112
所以你不需要去读一大段又一大段的文字，试图在脑子里同时记住五个不同的对比项，Notebook LM 会帮你把它们全部排列在整齐的行和列中。
So instead of reading through paragraph after paragraph, trying to hold five different comparisons in your head at once, Notebook LM lays it all out in neat rows and columns for you.

2374
03:03:44,272 --> 03:03:51,072
它会读取定性内容、描述、记录和解释，然后提取出实际的数据点并进行组织。
It reads the qualitative stuff, the descriptions, the write ups, the explanations, and it pulls out the actual data points and organizes them.

2375
03:03:51,232 --> 03:03:56,512
你可以在工作室面板里找到它，和其他工具一样。点击数据表，接下来是让它变得强大的部分。
You'll find it in the studio panel, same as the others. Click data table, and here's the part that makes it powerful.

2376
03:03:56,878 --> 03:04:01,792
你可以明确告诉它你想要哪些列，这样你就不用受限于它随机给你的内容了。
You can tell it exactly which columns you want, so you're not stuck with whatever it decides to give you.

2377
03:04:02,062 --> 03:04:07,312
你定义结构，它从源文件中填入行。而且它在这方面非常准确。
You define the structure and it fills in the rows from your sources. And it's genuinely accurate at this.

2378
03:04:07,472 --> 03:04:14,272
它会横向阅读你的材料，并将正确的细节放入对应的 Box 中，这能为你节省大量的手动分类工作。
It reads across your material and drops the right details into the right boxes, which saves you a huge amount of manual sorting.

2379
03:04:14,510 --> 03:04:23,312
这是一个体现它强大功能的典型例子。假设你上传了一堆文档，每一份都描述一个不同的工具、产品或研究。
Here's a clear example of when this really shines. Say you upload a handful of documents and each one describes a different tool, a different product, or a different study.

2380
03:04:23,472 --> 03:04:25,872
如果单独看，它们只是一个个独立的文字墙。
On their own, they're just separate walls of text.

2381
03:04:26,062 --> 03:04:29,632
而要对比它们，就意味着你得来回翻阅并手动做笔记。
And comparing them means flipping back and forth and taking notes by hand.

2382
03:04:29,806 --> 03:04:34,112
但如果你对所有这些内容生成一个数据表，它就会把所有内容并排对齐。
But run a data table across all of them and it lines everything up side by side.

2383
03:04:34,382 --> 03:04:42,032
你可以要求设置诸如名称、主要功能、优势和劣势等列，突然之间你就得到了一个可以一目了然查看的完整对比图表。
You could ask for columns like name, main features, strengths, and weaknesses, and suddenly you've got a full comparison chart you can read at a glance.

2384
03:04:42,222 --> 03:04:48,192
你也可以用它来建立时间轴表格，从长篇文档中提取出每一个关键日期和事件，并按顺序排列。
You could also use it to build a timeline table, pulling every key date and event out of a long document and stacking them in order.

2385
03:04:48,352 --> 03:04:53,392
或者将散落在报告中的特定事实提取到一个整齐的网格中。
Or to extract a specific set of facts scattered across a report into one tidy grid.

2386
03:04:53,486 --> 03:04:55,792
它不仅仅用于对比不同的文档。
And it's not only for comparing separate documents.

2387
03:04:55,952 --> 03:05:02,512
你可以指向一个长篇且内容密集的源文件，要求它将特定的细节提取到整洁的网格中。
You can point it at one long, dense source and ask it to pull out a specific set of details into a clean grid.

2388
03:05:02,672 --> 03:05:08,832
假设你有一份包含大量隐藏在段落中的数字的大型报告，你可以让它把每一个数字都提取出来并按类别组织。
Say you've got a big report full of numbers buried inside paragraphs, you can have it lift every figure out and organize it by category.

2389
03:05:08,992 --> 03:05:17,792
原本需要花一个小时去寻找和复制的内容，它能在瞬间完成，而且非常准确。而且这是这组工具中唯一能解决其他工具无法解决的问题的工具。
What would take you an hour of hunting and copying, it does in a moment, and it does it accurately. And this is the one tool of the bunch that solves a problem the others have.

2390
03:05:17,998 --> 03:05:20,912
数据表可以直接发送到 Google Sheets。
The data table can be sent straight to Google Sheets.

2391
03:05:21,072 --> 03:05:28,324
所以不同于抽认卡和测验（你只能截图），这是唯一一个你可以从 Notebook 中提取出来并继续处理的工具。
So unlike the flashcards and the quiz where you're stuck screenshotting, this is the one you can actually pull out of the notebook and keep working on.

2392
03:05:28,526 --> 03:05:34,592
一旦进入 Sheets，你就可以对它进行排序、筛选、添加自己的列，或者交给别人去处理。
Once it's in sheets, you can sort it, filter it, add your own columns, or hand it off to someone else.

2393
03:05:34,862 --> 03:05:39,300
当表格不是工作的终点而是起点时，这非常方便。
That makes it really handy when the table isn't the end of your work, it's the start of it.

2394
03:05:39,598 --> 03:05:42,672
关于数据表，我的建议可以归纳为两点。
My advice for the data table comes down to two things.

2395
03:05:42,832 --> 03:05:45,232
第一，要明确你的列。
First, be specific about your columns.

2396
03:05:45,486 --> 03:05:50,564
你对每一列想要的内容描述得越清晰，生成的表格就越整洁、更有用。
The clearer you are about what you want in each one, the cleaner and more useful the table comes out.

2397
03:05:50,830 --> 03:05:52,868
模糊的指令会给你一个模糊的表格。
Vague instructions give you a vague table.

2398
03:05:53,152 --> 03:05:58,592
第二，和工作室里的其他功能一样，只选择属于该对比项的源文件。
Second, like everything else in the studio, only select the sources that belong in that comparison.

2399
03:05:58,798 --> 03:06:03,952
取消勾选其余内容，这样表格就能保持聚焦，不会被无关的细节搞乱。
Leave the rest unchecked so the table stays focused and doesn't get cluttered with details that don't belong.

2400
03:06:04,112 --> 03:06:10,112
而且由于它导出非常整洁，养成习惯：只要有任何你想在后续继续构建的内容，就把它推送到 Sheets。
And since it exports so cleanly, get in the habit of pushing it to sheets whenever you've got something you'll want to build on later.

2401
