There are roadmaps that show you what to do first, second and third, and you get ready to use prompts.

2414
03:07:15,470 --> 03:07:21,872
这样你就能更快地从这个工具中获得优质的输出。说实话，这是从单纯观看转变为真正动手实践的最快途径。
So you pull great outputs out of this tool way faster. It's honestly the quickest way to stop just watching and start actually doing.

2415
03:07:22,126 --> 03:07:24,580
我会在最后告诉你具体如何加入。
And I'll tell you exactly how to jump in at the very end.

2416
03:07:24,752 --> 03:07:28,512
而我们清单上的最后一个，可能是最有趣的一个：信息图。
And the last one on our list is probably the most fun to look at, the infographic.

2417
03:07:28,782 --> 03:07:32,352
信息图能将你的源文件变成一个视觉化的摘要。
The infographic turns your sources into a single visual summary.

2418
03:07:32,512 --> 03:07:40,112
一张图片就能捕捉到核心观点、关键数据或不同想法之间的联系，而且这种格式非常便于一眼扫过。
One image that captures the main points, the key numbers, or the way different ideas connect, all in a format that's easy to take in at a glance.

2419
03:07:40,272 --> 03:07:45,952
当你想要快速理解某些内容时，它非常完美；而当你想要分享给其他人时，效果更棒。
It's perfect when you want to understand something quickly yourself, and it's even better when you want to share it with other people.

2420
03:07:46,192 --> 03:07:55,792
一张好的信息图能做到整页文字都难以做到的效果。现在，这是我真心希望你在点击之前稍微慢一点的工具。
A good infographic can do in one picture what a whole page of text struggles to do. Now, this is the one tool where I really want you to slow down for a second before you click.

2421
03:07:55,982 --> 03:08:00,352
在工作室面板中，你会看到信息图选项，但不要直接点击生成。
In the studio panel, you'll see the infographic option, but do not just hit generate.

2422
03:08:00,784 --> 03:08:03,024
先点击那个铅笔图标进行自定义。
Click that pencil icon first to customize it.

2423
03:08:03,184 --> 03:08:05,664
这比我在这部分说的任何话都重要。
This matters more than anything else I'll say in this section.

2424
03:08:05,870 --> 03:08:14,340
如果你跳过定制直接让它自动运行，它会随机为你选择设置。而这正是大多数令人失望的结果的来源。
If you skip the customizing and let it run on its own, it picks random settings for you. And that's exactly where most of the disappointing results come from.

2425
03:08:14,544 --> 03:08:19,184
一分钟的设置，就是你能自豪分享的作品和你最终删除的作品之间的区别。
A minute of setup is the difference between something you're proud to share and something you delete.

2426
03:08:19,470 --> 03:08:20,704
那么，你到底可以设置些什么呢？
So what can you actually set?

2427
03:08:20,864 --> 03:08:28,064
很多内容。你可以选择输出语言，可以选择详细程度：简洁、标准或详细，还可以设置比例
Quite a lot. You can choose your output language, you can pick the level of detail, concise, standard, or detailed, you can set the orientation,

2428
03:08:28,224 --> 03:08:31,344
正方形、纵向或横向，取决于你打算在什么地方使用它。
square, portrait, or landscape, depending on where you plan to use it.

2429
03:08:31,504 --> 03:08:35,332
还有你可以选择的视觉风格，或者让它自动选择为你匹配。
There are visual styles you can pick from, or you can let it auto select to look for you.

2430
03:08:35,566 --> 03:08:44,544
最后是功能最强大的控制项：文本框。在这里，你可以用自己的话描述你希望信息图展示什么内容，以及你希望它呈现出什么样的感觉。
And then there's the most powerful control of all, the text box, where you describe in your own words exactly what you want the infographic to show and how you want it to feel.

2431
03:08:44,782 --> 03:08:50,224
让我给你们举几个可以在那个框里输入的实际例子，因为这才是产生奇妙效果的关键所在。
Let me give you some real examples of what you can type into that box because this is where the magic happens.

2432
03:08:50,414 --> 03:08:58,704
在内容方面，你可以要求：根据这个源文件制作一个关键事件的时间线，或者对比文档中提到的优缺点。
On the content side, you could say create a timeline of the key events described in this source, or compare the pros and cons mentioned in the documents.

2433
03:08:58,894 --> 03:09:03,824
这些指令决定了最终出现在页面上的信息。然后你再来叠加视觉风格。
Those instructions shape what information ends up on the page. Then you can layer on the look.

2434
03:09:03,984 --> 03:09:13,104
你可以要求：使用蓝色调并突出显示三个关键数据，或者用更高级的描述，比如「便当式网格布局、简洁设计、专业配色」
You could say use a blue color theme and highlight the three key stats, or push the style further with something like bento grid layout, clean design, professional colours,

2435
03:09:13,344 --> 03:09:14,624
极简风格图标。
minimalist icons.

2436
03:09:14,862 --> 03:09:22,944
你甚至可以要求非常具体的审美：柔和的高科技感、手绘白板风、黑板质感，任何符合你传达信息的内容都可以。
You can even ask for very specific aesthetics: a soft, high-tech look, a hand-drawn whiteboard style, a chalkboard feel, whatever fits your message.

2437
03:09:23,118 --> 03:09:31,492
这个文本框就是让你的信息图从千篇一律的默认输出，变成真正脱颖而出且具有个人特色的作品的关键所在。
That text box is where your infographic goes from looking like everybody else's default output to something that actually stands out and feels like yours.

2438
03:09:31,758 --> 03:09:33,988
在生成之前，有一点值得注意。
Here's something worth knowing before you even generate.

2439
03:09:34,304 --> 03:09:38,464
信息图的质量很大程度上取决于源文件的清晰程度。
The quality of your infographic depends heavily on how clear your source is.

2440
03:09:38,638 --> 03:09:47,744
如果你的原始文档逻辑混乱、跳步或者因果关系混淆，那么生成的信息图也会显得很乱，因为它只能根据你提供的内容来工作。
If your original document jumps around, skips steps, or mixes up causes and effects, the infographic will look confused too, because it's only working with what you gave it.

2441
03:09:47,950 --> 03:09:51,184
所以如果你得到的结果很糟糕，别急着去怪工具。
So if you're getting messy results, don't blame the tool right away.

2442
03:09:51,344 --> 03:09:53,892
先看看源文件本身是否组织得当。
Take a look at whether the source itself is well organized.

2443
03:09:54,094 --> 03:09:55,812
输入清晰，输出才清晰。
Clean input, clean output.

2444
03:09:55,984 --> 03:10:01,984
这是工作室里所有工具的通用规律，但在视觉类内容上表现最明显，因为你可以直接看到页面上的混乱。
That's true for every tool in the studio, but it shows up the most with visuals because you can literally see the confusion on the page.

2445
03:10:02,144 --> 03:10:10,212
一旦设置好并点击生成，它就会在后台处理。所以你可以继续做别的事情，不用盯着加载界面等。
Once you've set it up and hit generate, it builds in the background. So you can keep working on other things while it does its thing. You don't have to sit and stare at a loading screen.

2446
03:10:10,384 --> 03:10:19,344
通常需要几分钟。准备好后，你可以用更大的查看器打开它，放大检查细节，然后下载为 PNG 文件并分享。
It usually takes a couple of minutes. When it's ready, you can open it up in a bigger viewer, zoom in to check the details, download it as a PNG file and share it.

2447
03:10:19,438 --> 03:10:25,344
如果效果接近但还不完美，你可以不断迭代，修改提示词，直到满意为止。
And if it's close but not quite right, you can iterate on it, tweak your prompt, and run it again until it lands.

2448
03:10:25,614 --> 03:10:27,984
不过关于输出结果有一点很重要。
There's one important thing to understand about the output though.

2449
03:10:28,206 --> 03:10:34,212
信息图生成出来的是静态的 PNG 图片。它是一个生成工具，不是图像编辑器。
The infographic comes out as a static PNG image. It's a generation tool, not an image editor.

2450
03:10:34,414 --> 03:10:40,260
所以你在 Notebook 里没法修改小错误、没法移动区块，也没法加上你自己的 Logo。
So inside the notebook, you can't fix a small typo, you can't move a block around, and you can't drop in your own logo.

2451
03:10:40,494 --> 03:10:47,424
如果你需要做这些修改，最好的办法是把 PNG 导入到 Canva 等设计工具中进行润色。
If you need to make those kinds of edits, the move is to pull the PNG into a design tool like Canva and clean it up there.

2452
03:10:47,504 --> 03:10:57,184
这里有个实用的专业技巧：如果你知道之后要去编辑它，就在提示词里要求使用纯白背景。比起复杂的纹理背景，编辑工具处理纯白背景的效果好得多。
A quick pro tip for that, if you know you're going to edit it later, ask for a plain white background in your prompt. Editing tools handle a clean white background way better than a busy textured one.

2453
03:10:57,264 --> 03:10:59,104
这样你的后期润色就会顺滑很多。
So your cleanup goes a lot smoother.

2454
03:10:59,310 --> 03:11:05,252
关于信息图，我的建议是：如果你打算分享到社交媒体上，请使用「简洁」模式。
Here's my advice for the infographic. If you're planning to share it on social media, use the concise setting.

2455
03:11:05,424 --> 03:11:11,424
它会减少文字量，提供更清爽、更易读的图像，方便人们在滑动时快速吸收内容。
It cuts down the text and gives you a cleaner, easier to read image that people can actually absorb while scrolling.

2456
03:11:11,598 --> 03:11:16,900
「详细」模式包含大量文本且字体很小，在手机上很难阅读。
The detailed setting packs in a lot of text with tiny fonts, which gets rough to read on a phone.

2457
03:11:17,184 --> 03:11:20,836
接下来，只选择你真正想要出现在视觉效果中的源文件。
Next, only select the sources you actually want in the visual.

2458
03:11:21,024 --> 03:11:25,904
如果你勾选了无关内容，会干扰设计并淡化核心信息。
If you leave irrelevant material checked, it confuses the design and dilutes the message.

2459
03:11:26,126 --> 03:11:28,544
最后，千万不要忽视那个文本提示词。
And finally, don't sleep on that text prompt.

2460
03:11:28,686 --> 03:11:36,100
默认设置也可以用，但那些能做出独特、出色信息图的人，都是在提示词里清晰描述他们想要的风格和重点。
The default settings are fine, but the people getting great unique infographics are the ones writing a clear description of the style and focus they want.

2461
03:11:36,304 --> 03:11:37,184
这就是核心所在。
That's the whole game.

2462
03:11:37,486 --> 03:11:43,744
让我把这些串联起来，因为它们各自承担不同的功能，一旦你搞清楚了区别，你就知道该选哪一个了。
Let me tie it all together, because they each do a different job, and once you know which is which, you'll always reach for the right one.

2463
03:11:44,014 --> 03:11:46,224
抽认卡和测验是你的学习组合。
Flashcards and the quiz are your study pair.

2464
03:11:46,414 --> 03:11:51,396
抽认卡把事实融入你的记忆，而测验则是测试你是否真的会用这些知识。
Flashcards push facts into your memory, and the quiz tests whether you can actually use them.

2465
03:11:51,630 --> 03:11:57,664
数据表是你的整理工具，能把杂乱的文本变成整齐的对比表，方便你导出并继续完善。
The data table is your organizer turning messy text into a clean comparison you can export and build on.

2466
03:11:57,838 --> 03:12:05,904
而信息图就是你的分享工具，它能把核心思想浓缩成一个视觉图形，方便你发给全世界。最棒的是，它们都是基于源内容的。
And the infographic is your sharer, wrapping the big ideas up in one visual you can send out into the world. And the best part, they're grounded in your own sources.

2467
03:12:05,984 --> 03:12:10,756
所以无论你得到什么结果，都始终与你的素材紧密相关，这意味着你可以信任它。
So whatever you get back always ties straight back to your material, which means you can trust it.

2468
03:12:10,944 --> 03:12:16,304
这就是从第一步点击到构建最终产出，如何使用 Gemini Notebook 的全过程。
So that is how you use Gemini Notebook from the very first click all the way to building your own outputs.

2469
03:12:16,494 --> 03:12:20,144
花点时间消化一下，因为你刚刚掌握了整套流程。
Take a second to let that actually sink in because you've just learned the whole thing.

2470
03:12:20,304 --> 03:12:28,464
你在左侧输入源文件，在中间通过对话与它们交流，然后在右侧的工作室面板中，将所有内容转化为真正有用的东西，
You feed it your sources on the left, you talk to them in the middle with the chat, and on the right in the studio panel, you turn all of it into something you can really use,

2471
03:12:28,544 --> 03:12:31,584
比如音频节目、思维导图、学习指南或完整的报告。
like an audio show, a mind map, a study guide, or a full report.

2472
03:12:31,984 --> 03:12:35,424
三个面板，一个简单的流程。这就是核心，现在你掌握它了。
Three panels, one simple flow. That's the heart of it, and now you know it.

2473
03:12:35,584 --> 03:12:44,704
最棒的是，要让这套系统运转并不需要任何技术背景。只要你会把文件放入文件夹并输入问题，你就已经具备了所有需要的技能。
And the best part is you don't need to be technical at all to make this work. If you can drop a file into a folder and type out a question, you already have every skill you need.

2474
03:12:44,814 --> 03:12:45,904
不需要学习任何代码。
There's no code to learn.

2475
03:12:46,126 --> 03:12:48,384
也不用去纠缠那些复杂的设置。
There are no messy settings to fight with.

2476
03:12:48,558 --> 03:12:54,464
你只需添加你的内容并开始提问。别忘了我们沿途提到的那些小功能，它们非常实用。
You just add your stuff and you start asking. And remember all those little extras we covered along the way because they really add up.

2477
03:12:54,670 --> 03:13:02,864
你可以通过勾选框开启或关闭源文件，让你的答案保持简洁聚焦。你还可以与队友共享 Notebook，甚至分享给整个团队。
You can turn sources on and off with those checkboxes to keep your answers tight and focused. You can share a notebook with a teammate or even open it up to a whole group.

2478
03:13:03,054 --> 03:13:07,104
你可以在遛狗时用手机把笔记听成播客一样。
You can listen to your notes like a podcast on your phone while you're out walking the dog.

2479
03:13:07,246 --> 03:13:16,464
而且有了新的云端计算机功能，它甚至可以运行真正的代码来挖掘你的数据、整合所有信息，你基本上拥有了一个永远不会疲倦的科研伙伴，
And with that new cloud computer feature, it can even run real code to dig into your data, put all of it together, and you've basically got a research partner that never gets tired,

2480
03:13:16,624 --> 03:13:19,104
它从不感到厌烦，也不会遗漏你的笔记。
never gets bored, and never loses track of your notes.

2481
03:13:19,344 --> 03:13:22,544
对于一个今天就能免费开启并使用的工具来说，这表现相当出色。
Not bad at all for something that's free to open up and start using today.

2482
03:13:22,766 --> 03:13:27,744
现在让我来回答一个我被问到最多的问题：到底谁需要这样的工具？
Now let me answer the question I get asked more than almost any other. Who actually needs a tool like this?

2483
03:13:27,904 --> 03:13:31,104
我的坦诚回答是：比大多数人想象的都要多。
And my honest answer is way more people than ever realize it.

2484
03:13:31,278 --> 03:13:39,524
你看，看到 Gemini Notebook 这个名字时，很容易就以为它是为工程师或数据极客设计的。但并不是这样，让我给你举几个例子。
See, it's really easy to look at something called Gemini Notebook and just assume it's built for engineers or data nerds. It isn't, so let me paint you a few pictures instead.

2485
03:13:39,790 --> 03:13:48,624
想象一下这个学生：他有一整学期的讲义、三本厚厚的教科书和一堆 PDF 文件，而且周一早上就要参加一场大型考试。
Picture the student who's got a whole semester of lecture notes, three fat textbooks, and a pile of PDFs with a big exam on Monday morning.

2486
03:13:48,782 --> 03:13:52,624
他可以把所有这些都放进去，到今晚就能拿到一份学习指南和一套测验。
They can drop all of it in and walk away with a study guide and a quiz by tonight.

2487
03:13:52,864 --> 03:14:00,784
想象一下这个企业主：他淹没在各种报告、合同和没完没了的邮件往来中，根本没时间去仔细阅读任何内容。
Picture the business owner who's drowning in reports, contracts, and never-ending email threads and never has time to read any of it properly.

2488
03:14:00,864 --> 03:14:05,184
他可以提出简单直接的问题，并在几秒钟内得到直接的答案。
They can ask plain, simple questions and get straight answers back in seconds.

2489
03:14:05,358 --> 03:14:11,104
想象一下这个研究人员：他在查阅 50 篇不同的研究，试图找到将它们全部联系起来的那一个关键发现。
Picture the researcher going through 50 different studies, trying to find the one finding that ties them all together.

2490
03:14:11,374 --> 03:14:19,344
想象一下这些作家或创作者：他们拥有多年积累的过往作品，正在寻找隐藏在其中的新鲜灵感。
Picture the writer or the creator sitting on years of their own old work, hunting for fresh ideas that are hiding in there somewhere.

2491
03:14:19,598 --> 03:14:22,384
而且这并不只针对忙碌的专业人士。
And it really doesn't stop with the busy professionals either.

2492
03:14:22,544 --> 03:14:29,904
想想那些从零开始学习全新领域，只想用通俗简单的语言来解释的人。
Think about the person learning a brand new subject completely from scratch, who just wants things explained to them in plain, simple words.

2493
03:14:30,190 --> 03:14:37,860
想想那些母语不是英语，需要把复杂难懂的文档拆解得平实清晰的人。
Think about someone who speaks English as a second language and needs a dense, complicated document broken down gently and clearly.

2494
03:14:38,094 --> 03:14:48,100
再想想那些试图让10个新员工快速上手，而不想每周重复解释上百遍的团队负责人。这些人其实都面临着同样的问题。
Think about a team leader who's trying to get 10 new hires up to speed without having to repeat themselves a hundred times a week. All of these people have the exact same problem sitting underneath.

2495
03:14:48,304 --> 03:14:51,236
信息量太大，而处理这些信息的时间又不够。
Too much information and not enough time to deal with it.

2496
03:14:51,406 --> 03:14:54,544
而这正是这个工具旨在解决的问题。
And that is precisely the problem this tool was built to solve.

2497
03:14:54,798 --> 03:14:57,344
这是我随着时间推移发现的一个有趣的小真相。
Here's the funny little truth I've noticed over time.

2498
03:14:57,584 --> 03:15:02,532
你感到越忙碌、越不知所措，这种工具带给你的回报就越多。
The busier and the more overwhelmed you feel, the more a tool like this actually gives back to you.

2499
03:15:02,766 --> 03:15:07,984
所以，如果这些场景哪怕有一点点符合你的生活，那么没错，这个工具绝对适合你。
So if any of those pictures looked even a little bit like your life, then yes, this is absolutely for you.

2500
03:15:08,238 --> 03:15:12,464
好，但在你急于去构建之前，让我先帮你避开一些坑。
Okay, but before you rush off and start building, let me protect you from the mistakes.

2501
03:15:12,624 --> 03:15:19,504
因为我看到很多人都在同样的几个问题上栽了跟头，而一些小的疏忽可能会让你根本无法体验到真正好的功能。
Because I've watched a lot of people trip over the same handful of things, and a few small slip-ups can stop you from ever reaching the really good stuff.

2502
03:15:19,694 --> 03:15:25,664
所以让我现在就帮你省掉一周的挫败感。第一个错误就是把所有内容都塞进一个巨大的 Notebook 里。
So let me save you a whole week of frustration right now. The first mistake is cramming everything into one giant notebook.

2503
03:15:25,904 --> 03:15:33,984
人们把工作项目、学校课题和一些随机的爱好全都放在同一个地方，然后奇怪为什么给出的答案模糊且混乱。
People throw a work project, a school subject, and some random hobby all into the same place, and then they wonder why the answers come out fuzzy and confused.

2504
03:15:34,064 --> 03:15:35,424
解决方法非常简单。
The fix is dead simple.

2505
03:15:35,584 --> 03:15:40,580
一个 Notebook 只对应一个主题，保持它们独立且清晰，你的答案就会变得精准。
One notebook, one topic, keep them separate and clean, and your answers get sharp again.

2506
03:15:40,846 --> 03:15:44,708
第二个错误是不加核实就相信每一个答案。
The second mistake is trusting every single answer without ever checking it.

2507
03:15:44,944 --> 03:15:51,264
现在，这个工具是基于源内容的，这很棒，但你仍然应该快速扫一眼那些引用。
Now, this tool is grounded in your sources, which is fantastic, but you should still take a quick glance at those citations.

2508
03:15:51,502 --> 03:15:57,664
它们之所以出现在每个答案旁边是有原因的。只需轻轻一点，就能看到那个答案到底来自哪里。
They sit right next to every answer for a reason. One little click shows you exactly where that answer came from.

2509
03:15:57,904 --> 03:16:02,544
养成这个习惯，你分享给别人的任何内容都会保持准确且有信心。
Make that a habit and you'll always stay accurate and confident in whatever you share with others.

2510
03:16:02,830 --> 03:16:07,984
第三个错误是把它当成普通的聊天机器人，去询问那些你根本没提供给它的内容。
The third mistake is treating it like a normal chatbot and asking it about things you never actually gave it.

2511
03:16:08,206 --> 03:16:10,864
记住，它不是整个互联网的搜索引擎。
Remember, this isn't a search engine for the whole entire internet.

2512
03:16:11,184 --> 03:16:13,184
它只知道你 Notebook 里的内容。
It only knows what's inside your notebook.

2513
03:16:13,358 --> 03:16:17,796
我知道这听起来像是个限制，但坦白说，这个限制正是它最大的优势。
And I know that sounds like a limit, but honestly, that limit is its single greatest strength.

2514
03:16:17,998 --> 03:16:22,304
这也是它不会像其他工具那样胡编乱造的根本原因。
It's the whole reason it doesn't just make things up the way other tools sometimes do.

2515
03:16:22,670 --> 03:16:26,148
第四个错误是害怕在导入后更改你的源文件。
The fourth mistake is being scared to change your sources once they're in.

2516
03:16:26,350 --> 03:16:30,084
人们添加几个文件，得到一个还可以的结果，然后就停止了。
People add a couple of files, get an okay result, and then they just stop.

2517
03:16:30,256 --> 03:16:36,496
但你随时可以回去，删掉弱相关的源文件，加入更好的内容，然后再重新生成你的输出。
But you can always go back, remove the weak sources, add some better ones, and then generate your outputs all over again.

2518
03:16:36,656 --> 03:16:39,296
这个工具就是为了让你去不断调整和塑造它的。
This thing is built for you to tinker with it and shape it.

2519
03:16:39,502 --> 03:16:44,256
你对选择源文件的投入越多，基于这些源文件构建出的内容就越出色。
The more care you put into picking your sources, the better everything you build on top of them turns out.

2520
03:16:44,462 --> 03:16:53,696
还有第五个错误，这个错误会让很多人损失惨重，那就是从未去碰工作室面板。很多人只用聊天功能，然后就到此为止了。
And the fifth mistake, the one that quietly costs people the very most, is never once touching the studio panel. So many folks only ever use the chat and then stop right there.

2521
03:16:53,856 --> 03:16:57,252
这有点像买了一整套工具箱，却只用其中的锤子。
That's a bit like buying a whole toolbox and only ever using the hammer.

2522
03:16:57,486 --> 03:17:07,056
真正的魔力在于把你的源文件变成音频、视觉化的思维导图、抽认卡和学习指南。如果你跳过所有这些，你就错过了这整套工具最好的一半功能。
The real magic is turning your sources into audio, into a visual mind map, into flashcards and study guides. If you skip all of that, you're missing the best half of the entire tool.

2523
03:17:07,136 --> 03:17:08,896
所以请务必去好好探索一下。
So please go and explore it properly.

2524
03:17:09,166 --> 03:17:13,856
现在，这一切引出一个我内心深处非常相信的观点，我想花点时间和大家分享一下。
Now all of this leads me to something I really believe deep down, and I want to take a moment to share it with you.

2525
03:17:14,016 --> 03:17:19,456
当你以正确的方式使用 AI 时，它并不是来取代你的，而是为了让你的工作变得更轻松。
When you use AI the right way, it is not here to replace you. It's here to make your work easier.

2526
03:17:19,536 --> 03:17:26,016
我之所以这么说，是因为我知道很多人对 AI 有点紧张，觉得它好像在威胁他们的工作或创造力。
And I say that because I know a lot of people feel a little nervous about AI, like it's somehow coming for their job or their creativity.

2527
03:17:26,222 --> 03:17:30,628
但像这样的工具根本不是干这个的。让我具体解释一下我的意思。
But that is not what a tool like this does at all. So let me explain exactly what I mean.

2528
03:17:30,896 --> 03:17:36,896
稍微想想你典型的一天。有多少时间被那些缓慢、乏味、重复性的琐事给消耗掉了？
Just think about your typical day for a second. How much of it gets eaten up by slow, boring, repetitive stuff.

2529
03:17:37,056 --> 03:17:46,336
为了找一个微小的细节而去读长篇大论，去翻找堆满文件的文件夹，一遍又一遍地写同样的摘要，或者把笔记从一个地方复制到另一个地方。
Reading long pages just to find one little fact, sorting through folders full of files, writing the same kind of summary over and over again, copying notes from one place to another.

2530
03:17:46,496 --> 03:17:51,536
这些都不是真正的核心工作。这些是挡在真正工作面前的杂事。
None of that is the real work. That's the busy work that piles up in front of the real work.

