05:45:37,934 --> 05:45:43,184
让我带你了解驱动 Gemini Spark 的三件事：任务、技能和计划。
Let me walk you through the three things that power Gemini Spark, tasks, skills, and schedules.

4604
05:45:43,264 --> 05:45:47,780
因为一旦你理解了这三点，你就会明白它为什么与市面上其他的 AI 工具完全不同。
Because once you understand these three, you'll see exactly why this is different from every other AI tool out there.

4605
05:45:47,984 --> 05:45:49,504
任务是起点。
Tasks are the starting point.

4606
05:45:49,664 --> 05:45:55,984
任务是你交给 Spark 的一个多步骤目标，而不是一两句简单的话，比如“帮我写个文案”，而是一个真正的目标。
A task is a multi-step goal you hand to Spark, not a one-liner, not write me a caption, a real objective,

4607
05:45:56,206 --> 05:46:04,944
比如“在接下来的两周内寻找并跟踪我所在行业的招聘信息”，或者“检查我的收件箱，找出所有提到交付物的邮件，并将它们全部放入一个 Google Doc 中”。
something like find and track job listings in my industry for the next two weeks, or go through my inbox, pull out every email that mentions a deliverable, and put it all in a Google Doc.

4608
05:46:05,262 --> 05:46:14,064
Spark 会接收这些任务并从头到尾处理。它可以搜索网络、阅读你的 Google Drive、提取 Gmail 信息、更新 Sheets，涵盖多个步骤，且全由它自动完成。
Spark takes that and handles it from start to finish. It can search the web, read through your Google Drive, pull from Gmail, update sheets, all across multiple steps, all on its own.

4609
05:46:14,254 --> 05:46:23,556
而且因为它与你的 Google Workspace 原生连接，包括 Gmail、Calendar、Drive、Docs、Sheets 和 Slides，所以它能真正访问你的数据，而不仅仅是表面上的摘要。
And because it's connected to your Google Workspace natively, Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, it has actual access to your data, not a surface level summary.

4610
05:46:23,854 --> 05:46:25,504
技能是让它变得非常强大的地方。
Skills are where it gets really powerful.

4611
05:46:25,710 --> 05:46:31,076
技能是你创建一次即可重复使用的指令集，Spark 每当相关时就会应用它。
A skill is a reusable instruction set you build once, and then Spark applies it every time it's relevant.

4612
05:46:31,342 --> 05:46:31,824
想象一下这个场景。
Picture this.

4613
05:46:32,078 --> 05:46:39,620
你要求 Spark 阅读你最近发出的 50 封邮件，搞清楚你的写作风格，根据这些建立一个风格指南，并将其作为名为 Ghostwriter 的技能保存下来。
You ask Spark to read your last 50 outgoing emails, figure out how you write, build a style guide from that, and then save it as a skill called Ghostwriter.

4614
05:46:39,824 --> 05:46:43,584
从那时起，每当你要求 Spark 起草内容时，它都会用你的语气来写。
From that point on, every time you ask Spark to draft something, it writes in your voice.

4615
05:46:43,744 --> 05:46:46,464
这不仅仅是自动化，而是带有上下文的自动化。
That's not just automation, that's automation with context.

4616
05:46:46,670 --> 05:46:53,604
你可以使用 @ 符号或斜杠命令来调用技能，或者当 Spark 判断相关时，它会自动调入这些技能。
You can call up skills using the at symbol or the slash command, or Spark can pull them in automatically when it figures out they're relevant.

4617
05:46:53,838 --> 05:46:59,984
计划是第三个环节。这是将 Spark 从一个单次任务执行者转变为真正的后台操作者的关键。
Schedules are the third piece. This is how you turn Spark from a one-time task runner into a true background operator.

4618
05:47:00,238 --> 05:47:04,864
计划允许你为 Spark 设置基于时间的或基于事件的触发器，让它自动启动。
A schedule lets you set time-based or event-based triggers for Spark to kick off automatically.

4619
05:47:05,070 --> 05:47:13,156
例如：每周一早上 9 点，扫描我的收件箱，总结上周发生的情况，提取最重要的待办事项，并在我的 Calendar 上预留深度工作的时间。
For example, every Monday at 9 a.m., scan my inbox, summarize what happened last week, pull out the most important action items, and block time on my calendar for deep work.

4620
05:47:13,344 --> 05:47:18,144
